+ Register of Deeds 
+ Welcome to the Horry County Register of Deeds website! 
+ As the custodian of land records for Horry County, South Carolina, we are committed to providing efficient and transparent access to vital property information for our community members. Whether you're a homeowner, real estate professional, or researcher, our comprehensive database and resources are here to assist you. 
+ Horry County Register of Deeds Customer Service and Recording Desk Will close at  3:30PM  on Tuesday, June 30, 2026 In order to complete the 2026 Fiscal Year-End Closing All public rooms will remain open 
+ Responsibilities 
+ Land Records 
+ Recording Information 
+ Records Research 
+ Our office meticulously maintains and preserves a vast array of land records, including deeds, mortgages, plats, and other pertinent documents essential for property transactions and ownership verification. Whether you're searching for historical deeds or the most recent property transactions, our user-friendly system makes it easy to access the information you need. 
+ For individuals or entities involved in property transactions, our office provides a streamlined process for recording deeds, mortgages, and other related documents. Our knowledgeable staff ensures that each document is accurately recorded and securely stored, maintaining the integrity of property ownership records for future generations. 
+ Researchers and genealogists will find our office to be a valuable resource for exploring Horry County's rich history through property records. Whether you're tracing the lineage of a family homestead or conducting academic research, our archives offer a wealth of information waiting to be discovered. Our dedicated staff is available to assist with research inquiries and provide guidance on navigating our extensive collection of records. 
+ Recording and Service Fee Change 
+ On May 16, 2019 the Governor signed Bill H3243. This act amended Section 8-21-310 of the South Carolina Code of Laws as it relates to the schedule of recording fees used in South Carolina. These fees will be effective beginning August 1, 2019.
+ This will remove the current per page fees used for recordings, and instead create flat fees used to record the majority of documents. This amendment will affect the recording fees of all documents as well. It will also involve the creation of a separate recording fee for any deed relating to a title of interest in a vacation time sharing plan. However, in order to record a document as such the deed must include clear notice on the first page and be titled ‘Vacation Time Sharing Ownership Deed’. If not titled this way the document will be rejected due to not meeting the recording requirements defined in the State Statute.
+ Due to this amendment the Horry County Register of Deeds schedule of fees has changed. As such we are posting the updated fee schedule as it will exist beginning at 8am on August 1st.
+ Links 
+ Price 
+ Bill H3243 
+ UCC Filings 
+ Amendments to UCC Article 9 are effective July 1, 2013, as a result of S.323 signed into law on June 7, 2013. The changes are a result of the 2010 Amendments to Article 9 from the Uniform Law Commission and adopted by the International Association of Commercial Administrators (IACA) which were to become effective July 1, 2013.
+ Forms submitted for recording must be dated July 1, 2013. Approved forms can be downloaded from the South Carolina Secretary of State website.
+ The law governing the change can be found on the South Carolina Legislature website.
