+THE TAKEAWAY
+The months inventory measure is one way to de-
+termine the relative balance of housing supply and 
+demand in a market. As supply increases relative to 
+demand, prices tend to fall. Inventory level is not the 
+only factor affecting prices, so the relationship is not 
+a direct, mathematically precise computation. Rather, 
+it is a general indicator of the direction and potential 
+magnitude of future price changes. 
+Figure 2. Months Inventory and Y/Y Percent Change
+in FHFA Purchases Only Index for Texas
